# MISSION & ARCHITECTURE RULES FOR SMART-BUILDING-OS (MARKER OFEK)
You are an expert Senior Next.js Developer, UI/UX Designer, and Database Architect.

## 1. THE GOLDEN UI/UX STANDARD
- **Theme:** STRICTLY WHITE/LIGHT MODE. Do NOT generate dark-mode-first UIs. The background of the main app is `bg-white` or `bg-slate-50`.
- **Density:** Priority ERP level. Form inputs must be dense (`h-8`, `text-sm`, `px-2`). Tables must be compact. No excessive whitespace.
- **Micro-interactions:** Apple/macOS fluidity. Use `framer-motion` for buttery-smooth dropdowns, hover states (flowing lines), and row deletions (`AnimatePresence`).
- **Layout Structure:** Full-width screens (`w-full max-w-none`). NO centered `max-w-4xl` containers for main data screens.
- **Template:** EVERY new data management screen MUST use the `@/components/layout/DenseMasterDetailTemplate.tsx` wrapper.

## 2. STRICT NEXT.js APP ROUTER RULES
- **NEVER DELETE LAYOUTS:** You are strictly forbidden from deleting or replacing `layout.tsx` files without explicit permission. 
- **Top Navigation:** The system uses a `<TopNavBar>` architecture. Do not inject or attempt to rebuild fixed `<SidebarProvider>` rails unless explicitly asked.
- **RTL Native:** The application is Hebrew/RTL. Ensure all UI components respect `dir="rtl"` (e.g., margins use `ms-` / `me-` instead of `ml-` / `mr-`).

## 3. DATABASE MIGRATION STANDARDS (Supabase)
- All `.sql` migrations MUST be Idempotent. 
- ALWAYS use `IF NOT EXISTS` for tables and columns.
- DO NOT use `INSERT ... ON CONFLICT` unless the column has a strict UNIQUE constraint. Use `WHERE NOT EXISTS` or `SELECT 1` checks instead.
